# Cursor Editor — Collaborative Editing

## Overview

Cursor supports collaborative editing through integration with VS Code Live Share and native team features. This document covers how AI agents behave in collaborative contexts, shared vs independent agent sessions, and best practices for pair programming with Cursor.

---

## Collaborative Editing Features

### VS Code Live Share Integration

Cursor inherits VS Code's Live Share capabilities for real-time collaboration:

| Feature | Live Share Support | Cursor AI Impact |
|---------|-------------------|-----------------|
| **Real-time editing** | ✅ Yes | Each participant has their own AI context |
| **Shared cursors** | ✅ Yes | AI sees all cursor positions |
| **Shared terminals** | ✅ Yes | AI can execute in shared terminal |
| **Shared debugging** | ✅ Yes | AI assists debugging sessions |
| **Audio/video** | ✅ Yes (external) | Not integrated with Cursor AI |

### Team Collaboration Workflows

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Host creates Live Share session] --> B[Invite participants]
    B --> C[Participants join]
    C --> D{AI collaboration model}
    
    D --> E[Shared AI session]
    D --> F[Independent AI sessions]
    
    E --> G[One agent serves all participants]
    F --> H[Each participant has own agent]
    
    G --> I[Shared context, synchronized]
    H --> J[Independent context per person]
```

