## Privacy in Multiplayer

### What Each Participant Can See

| Information | Visible to | Reason |
|------------|-----------|--------|
| **Your prompts** | You only | Private to your Composer session |
| **Your agent responses** | You only | Private to your session |
| **Your agent output** | You only | Debug info is personal |
| **File edits** | All participants | Live Share syncs files |
| **Terminal commands** | Terminal owner (or shared if shared) | Terminal sharing setting |
| **Your cursor position** | All participants (if shared cursors on) | Live Share feature |
| **Your open files** | Host (if host view enabled) | Live Share feature |

### Privacy Controls

```json
{
  // Live Share settings (inherited from VS Code)
  "livestream.participantCanSeeMyFiles": false,
  "livestream.participantCanSeeMyCursors": false,
  
  // Hide sensitive data in shared sessions
  "cursor.agent.privateContext": true,
  
  // Don't share terminal output
  "terminal.sharedOutput": false
}
```

### Sensitive Context in Collaboration

When collaborating, be aware:

1. **Agent prompts may be visible** if shared terminal is used
2. **Agent responses may leak** code patterns from private sessions
3. **@-references in shared context** are visible to all
4. **Custom instructions** are personal, not shared

**Best Practice**: Never include sensitive information (API keys, secrets, PII) in prompts during collaborative sessions.

